 ## Overview
-Focus and Context Multiresolution Rendering is a technique to balance processing capacity between a high-detail focus region and a lower-detail context region to improve interactivity in time-critical applications [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from sibling methods like [Level-of-detail (LOD) methods](1007-level-of-detail-lod-methods.md) by explicitly separating the scene into two distinct rendering passes with different resolutions and complexity levels, rather than adapting a single view's resolution based on distance or error metrics. The goal is not seamless integration but a tradeoff between achievable quality and speed [S1, unofficial].
+Focus and Context Multiresolution Rendering is a technique that balances processing capacity between a high-detail "focus" region and a lower-detail "context" region to improve interactivity in time-critical volume rendering applications [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from sibling methods like [Level-of-detail (LOD) methods](1007-level-of-detail-lod-methods.md) by explicitly separating the scene into two distinct rendering passes with different resolutions and rendering models, rather than adapting a single representation based on distance or error metrics. The goal is not seamless integration but a trade-off between achievable quality and speed [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
